NetPrint prints over the network to an AirPrint printer that takes URF, from
anything that uses the RISC OS printer drivers, such as !Draw and !Edit.

Run it once, fill in the printer's address and pick the paper. Save keeps both
on a VMU. It has to stay on the icon bar, as it does the job of !Printers. Print
as usual from any application, or drop a text file on the icon. Test page shows
that it all works.
